  "VERDICT": {
    "targeted_reduce_bare_ce": false,
    "random_increase_bare_ce": true,
    "dissociation_survives_wrapper_removal": false,
    "READING": "The dissociation does NOT survive removal of the chat-wrapper in the form originally stated. Under the bare pinned lm-eval context NO method improves final-answer CE: every arm degrades it relative to base (targeted +0.28 to +0.53, Random +1.01 to +1.21). The CE *improvement* seen in D2 was therefore specific to the operational target-pipeline serialization (the LlamaFactory [INST] wrapper), i.e. it is an improvement on the surrogate as the targeting pipeline actually computes it, not on final-answer cross-entropy in the serialization the task metric uses.",
    "scope_note": "This is the LAST forensic diagnostic. No protocol, method, or result changes follow from it.",
    "separation_preserved": true,
    "max_targeted_bare_delta": 0.5281193279661238,
    "min_random_bare_delta": 1.007408873643726,
    "WHAT_SURVIVES": "Two things do survive and are what the paper should claim. (1) The targeted/Random SEPARATION is preserved and is strictly ordered: every target-aware method degrades bare-context CE far less (max +0.53) than either Random control (min +1.01), and the within-group ordering is unchanged -- so the selectors demonstrably move the model toward the query set in BOTH serializations, they simply do not reach an absolute improvement in the bare one. (2) The task-metric direction is unchanged: on the same 64 items every method's CoT exact-match falls, and the targeted methods are the ones that lose most downstream.",
    "REQUIRED_SCOPING": "The claim must be scoped to the EXACT OPERATIONAL TARGETING SURROGATE (wrapped final-answer CE), not to cross-entropy generically. Correct statement: 'the surrogate actually used by the targeting pipeline improves on the very examples that define the target while the task metric on those same examples does not; we do NOT attribute the mismatch to cross-entropy independent of prompt serialization.' Any sentence implying 'final-answer CE per se is misaligned with CoT generation' is not supported and must not be written.",
    "value_of_this_check": "This is exactly why the check was worth running: it falsified the broader version of our own claim before a reviewer could. Reported as a negative result rather than dropped."
  }
}